MISSING symbol versions in ROOT/:

  libfoo.so.1: FOO_2
      needed by usr/bin/app
      needed by usr/bin/app1
      needed by usr/bin/app2
      needed by usr/bin/app3
      ... and 3 more

These binaries were compiled against a newer library than the image ships and will
fail at exec time. For glibc that means the build didn't go through our sysroot:
check that SYSROOT reaches the compiler (builder/build-package.sh) and that the
package's build system doesn't drop the CFLAGS/LDFLAGS it exports.
